  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field of an electromagnetic wave in free space is represented as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>. The corresponding magnetic induction vector will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
      "is_correct": false
